KG42.register("rules-31fc2f235da5f109a5660839",{"id":"41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R009","paper":"41-data_center_local_markets","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R009","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The local-market cost/revenue equals the CSP’s proposed signed purchase/selling price multiplied by the smaller of its absolute net-load energy and its estimated trading volume. A positive amount represents purchase cost; a negative amount represents selling revenue of the corresponding absolute value. Scope: The CSP’s modeled cost/revenue in the kth local energy market at the tth time slot.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["settlement.payment"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"The CSP’s modeled cost/revenue in the kth local energy market at the tth time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E08"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x-piT","symbol":"\\pi_k^T(t)","meaning":"Energy purchase/selling price proposed by the CSP in the kth local energy market at the tth time slot; positive denotes a purchase price and negative denotes a selling price under the source sign convention.","kind":"operational","domain":"signed real price in $/kWh; positive purchase and negative selling per source sign convention","unit":"$/kWh","indices":["k","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E04"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x-ET","symbol":"E_k^T(t)","meaning":"Estimated energy purchase/selling volume under the proposed price \\pi_k^T(t) in the kth local energy market at the tth time slot.","kind":"operational","domain":"non-negative real energy volume, E_k^T(t) \\ge 0 per source","unit":"kWh","indices":["k","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E04"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x-PN","symbol":"P_k^N(t)","meaning":"Net-load of the kth IDC at the tth time slot; positive means the IDC needs to buy energy from external sources and negative means surplus energy to sell.","kind":"operational","domain":"signed real power in kW","unit":"kW","indices":["k","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g02-E07"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x-CDEM","symbol":"C_k^{DEM}(t)","meaning":"Cost/revenue of the CSP in the kth local energy market at the tth time slot; positive represents purchase cost and negative represents selling revenue of |C_k^{DEM}(t)|.","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued monetary cost/revenue in $, defined by Eq. (14)","unit":"$","indices":["k","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E08"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-DeltaT","symbol":"\\Delta T","meaning":"Duration of each time slot (hour) in the modeled operation horizon.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"hour","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E07"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The local-market cost/revenue equals the CSP’s proposed signed purchase/selling price multiplied by the smaller of its absolute net-load energy and its estimated trading volume. A positive amount represents purchase cost; a negative amount represents selling revenue of the corresponding absolute value. Scope: The CSP’s modeled cost/revenue in the kth local energy market at the tth time slot.","expression":"C_k^{DEM}(t) = \\pi_k^T(t) \\cdot \\min\\left\\{\\left|P_k^N(t)\\cdot\\Delta T\\right|, E_k^T(t)\\right\\}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-x-piT","v141-c-R009-x-ET","v141-c-R009-x-PN","v141-c-R009-x-CDEM"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-theta-DeltaT"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E08"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-307a684414-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1.3 Energy trading cost/revenue from the local energy markets","anchor_text":"3.1.3. Energy trading cost/revenue from the local energy markets For each IDC, its net-load at the t","equation_id":"Eq. (14)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"$P_k^N(t)=P_k^{IDC}(t)+P_k^{CH/DIS}(t)-P_k^{RES}(t)$ (12)\n$P_k^{RES}(t)=\\beta_k^{RES}(t)\\cdot P_k^{RES}$ (13)\nA positive value of $P_k^N(t)$ indicates that the IDC needs to buy energy from external sources (i.e. the local energy market and/or the grid), while a negative value indicates that the IDC has surplus energy to sell to other customers. On the basis of the CSP’s proposed energy purchase/selling price in the kth local energy market, the corresponding amount of energy that the CSP can buy from/sell to the market can be estimated following Eq. (7). Then, the cost/revenue of the CSP from the kth local energy market is calculated as:\n$C_k^{DEM}(t)=\\pi_k^T(t)\\cdot\\min\\left\\{|P_k^N(t)\\cdot\\Delta T|, E_k^T(t)\\right\\}$ (14)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E08","location":{"location_id":"src-307a684414-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1.3 / 3.1.4 Energy trading and grid purchase costs","anchor_text":"C. Guo et al. Consisting with the sign of πTk(t), when CDEMk (t) is positive, it repre­ sents the CS","equation_id":"Eq. (15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Consisting with the sign of $\\pi_k^T(t)$, when $C_k^{DEM}(t)$ is positive, it represents the CSP’s energy purchase cost in the kth local energy market at the tth time slot; when it is negative, it means that the CSP sells energy to the market with the revenue of $|C_k^{DEM}(t)|$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-307a684414-p02-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"PpVariables PiAk(t) Number of requests arriving at the kth IDC in the tth time PU slot εkBk(t) Numbe","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"πTk(t) Energy purchase/selling price proposed by the CSP in the kth local energy market in the tth time slot ($/kWh); ETk(t) Estimated energy purchase/selling volume under πTk(t)(kWh); CDEMk(t) Cost/revenue in the kth local energy market in the tth time slot ($); PNk(t) Net-load of the kth IDC at the tth time slot (kW); εk(t) Price-demand elasticity factor of the kth IDC in the tth time slot; πT0k(t) Reference energy purchase/selling price in the kth local energy market in the tth time slot ($); ET0k(t) Reference energy demand under πT0k(t)(kWh); πRETk Electricity retail price at the kth region ($); PLk Capacity of the power line connecting the kth IDC and the grid (kW)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-307a684414-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Price-demand elasticity model","anchor_text":"estimated as: 3. εk(t)ET0k (t)ETk (t) = πTk (t) + (1 −εk(t))ET0k (t) (7) πT0k (t) PNk Without loss o","equation_id":"Eq. (7)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In each time slot, the CSP proposes energy purchase/selling prices to other participants in the local energy markets, either through auction-based mechanisms or P2P negotiations. Under an energy purchase/selling price, the amount of energy that the CSP can purchase from/sell to the market can be estimated through a price-demand elasticity model (Eq. (6)), which describes the relationship between the price signal and the demand. \\epsilon_k(t)=\\frac{(E_k^T(t)-E_k^{T0}(t))/E_k^{T0}(t)}{(\\pi_k^T(t)-\\pi_k^{T0}(t))/\\pi_k^{T0}(t)},\\quad E_k^{T0}(t)\\ne0 \\tag{6} E_k^T(t)=\\frac{\\epsilon_k(t)E_k^{T0}(t)}{\\pi_k^{T0}(t)}\\pi_k^T(t)+(1-\\epsilon_k(t))E_k^{T0}(t) \\tag{7} Obviously, ε_k(t) is positive when the CSP purchases energy, and is negative when it sells energy in the kth local energy market. Without loss of generality, we use positive and negative values of π_k^T(t) to indicate the energy purchase and selling price proposed by the CSP in the local energy market, respectively. The energy purchase/selling demand E_k^T(t) is a non-negative value."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-307a684414-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Price-demand elasticity model","anchor_text":"estimated as: 3. εk(t)ET0k (t)ETk (t) = πTk (t) + (1 −εk(t))ET0k (t) (7) πT0k (t) PNk Without loss o","equation_id":"Eq. (7)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Without loss of generality, we use positive and negative values of $\\pi_k^T(t)$ to indicate the energy purchase and selling price proposed by the CSP in the local energy market, respectively. The energy purchase/selling demand $E_k^T(t)$ is a non-negative value."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E07","quote":"$C_k^{DEM}(t)=\\pi_k^T(t)\\cdot\\min\\left\\{|P_k^N(t)\\cdot\\Delta T|, E_k^T(t)\\right\\}$ (14)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E08","quote":"when $C_k^{DEM}(t)$ is positive, it represents the CSP’s energy purchase cost in the kth local energy market at the tth time slot; when it is negative, it means that the CSP sells energy to the market with the revenue of $|C_k^{DEM}(t)|$."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"c11c6b18658e6df6bc6f13cf2a4d33c8f56d0d28dbfe1875caa6ea50bcbaa128","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Source Eq. (14) defines settlement.payment as C_k^DEM(t)=π_k^T(t)·min{|P_k^N(t)·ΔT|, E_k^T(t)}, and the accompanying text assigns positive values to purchase cost and negative values to selling revenue. C.1 froze V={settlement.payment} with E=[]; the relation is a unary definition, so no graph edge is required. C.1 supplied x=[] and theta=[]; C.2 adds the source-defined quantities used by Eq. (14) with same-mechanism evidence. B evidence remains unreviewed in this experiment, so this formalization is provisional and not an independent source audit.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-x-piT","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"\\pi_k^T(t) is the signed price factor inside the settlement.payment formula Eq. (14); the frozen graph has no typed edge for this unary function, so it binds to the only existing node."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-x-ET","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"E_k^T(t) is the estimated traded volume entering the min{} expression of settlement.payment Eq. (14)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-x-PN","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"P_k^N(t) supplies the absolute net-load energy term |P_k^N(t)·ΔT| in settlement.payment Eq. (14)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-x-CDEM","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C_k^{DEM}(t) is the cost/revenue value produced by settlement.payment Eq. (14)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-DeltaT","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"\\Delta T converts net-load power to net-load energy in settlement.payment Eq. (14)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Constraint C001 is the source Eq. (14) definition of the settlement.payment relation; no E edges exist in the frozen graph for this unary function."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
